sition and control, and I9 does this well.\n\nSo, I’ve decided on I9, this restricts the diagonal to the opponent.\n\nMy move is: {"col": "I", "row": 9}\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: The game has just begun with Black playing the first move at the center of the board (H8). As White, there are no immediate threats to block. The optimal strategy is to place a stone adjacent to the Black stone to disrupt their potential continuous lines and establish a presence in the center. Common and strong responses are playing straight adjacent (like H9 or I8) or diagonally adjacent (like I9 or G7). Playing diagonally is a classic opening tactic to restrict the opponent\'s diagonal power, which can be dangerous in Gomoku.\n\nReason: I9 is a standard diagonal attachment to the center stone H8. It effectively challenges Black\'s control of the center and prepares White for both defensive blocking and offensive line-building in the diagonals.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "I", "row": 9}'}
